# THIRD-PARTY DOCUMENTATION IS NOT OURS TO REDISTRIBUTE.
#
# docs/ doubles as the working reference shelf for this project: Keithley's DMM6500 manuals and TSP app
# examples, Siglent's generator and scope programming guides, and a couple of processor reference manuals.
# They are what the measurements were made against and they are cited throughout the code, but they are
# vendor copyright and this repository is public -- so they stay local. Every number they were used to
# establish is quoted, with its source named, in docs/REFERENCE.md.
#
# Listed by vendor rather than by a blanket docs/*.txt rule, so a document WE write in docs/ is published
# by default instead of silently disappearing.

# Keithley
docs/DMM6500_*.txt
docs/DMM6500-*.txt
docs/DMM6500DisplayDoc.md
docs/Display API Command Reference.md
docs/Keithley_DMM6500_Notes-*.txt
docs/1KW-*.txt
docs/2000SCAN-*.txt
docs/K10SCAN_schematic.txt
docs/LowLevelHandbook_*.txt
docs/TSPAPP-*.txt
docs/TSPAPP_*.txt

# Siglent (generator and scope)
docs/SDG_*.pdf
docs/SDG_*.txt
docs/SDG2000X_*.pdf
docs/SDG2000X_*.txt
docs/SDS1000*.pdf
docs/SDS1000*.txt
docs/SDS1002X-*.pdf
docs/SDS1002X-*.txt

# Processor reference manuals
docs/Arm-Cortex-M4-Processor-Datasheet.txt
docs/e300coreRM.txt
docs/MPC5125RM.txt

# BENCH OUTPUT IS EVIDENCE, NOT SOURCE: regenerable by re-running the harness, tens of megabytes of it,
# and it dates immediately.
out/

# THE WORKING LOG STAYS LOCAL. notes/ is a session-by-session engineering journal -- bench wiring, IP
# addresses, firmware quirks, review transcripts, what was tried and abandoned. It is the most useful file
# in the project to whoever is holding the probe and the least useful to whoever is reading the code, and
# publishing it would put a lot of unreviewed detail about a specific bench on the open web. Everything a
# reader needs is in docs/REFERENCE.md, which is written to be read.
notes/

# Local tooling and OS noise
.claude/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
